tests {
  // Protrack returns HTTP 200 with a non-zero `code` on every failure (expired token,
  // unauthorised IMEI, blocked account), so the status code alone proves nothing.
  test("envelope code is 0", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getBody().code, JSON.stringify(res.getBody())).to.equal(0);
  });
}

docs {
  # Protrack365 Open API

  Direct, **read-only** calls to the Protrack365 GPS platform (not a Vahn service), used to work out
  the response shapes before building the `protrack365` polling adapter in `location-service`.
  Vendor doc: https://www.protrack365.com/api.jsp

  ## Credentials

  Read from `bruno/collections/protrack365/.env` (gitignored). Create it locally:

  ```
  PROTRACK365_ACCOUNT=<account>
  PROTRACK365_PASSWORD=<raw password>
  ```

  ## Token

  `auth/authorization` computes `signature = md5(md5(password) + time)` in a pre-request script and
  stores the token with `bru.setVar` (a runtime var), so it is **never written to the env file**.
  Run it first in the app; the CLI runs the whole collection in `seq` order:

  ```bash
  npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/collections/protrack365 --env staging
  ```

  Issuing a token **invalidates the previous one** for the account. Anything else polling this
  account (e.g. location-service once the adapter is live) loses its token when you run this.

  `device/list` captures the account's IMEIs into `protrackImeis` / `protrackImei` for the later
  requests. Blank both in `environments/staging.bru` before committing.

  The vendor has one environment; `staging.bru` exists only to match the repo convention.

  ## Deliberately not included

  `command/send` (includes `RELAY,1` = cut the engine), geofence create/edit/delete,
  user block/unblock and password set all act on the customer's live fleet. Do not add them here.
}
